== Why the provider-only bundle reports 2 file(s), 642 MB ==
# measured 2026-11-27 on the RTX 3060 machine, ONNX Runtime 1.20.1 GPU package
# (.validation/ort-gpu-1.20.1) against the ORT 1.32.0 package beside it.

$ sha1sum the shipped provider against the upstream package file
17cdf92693575e1351d92cce9f70cf1b08a7ad0a *.validation/ort-gpu-1.20.1/bin/onnxruntime_providers_cuda.dll
17cdf92693575e1351d92cce9f70cf1b08a7ad0a *templates/onnx-inference-ofx/build/bundle/OnnxInference.ofx.bundle/Contents/Win64/onnxruntime_providers_cuda.dll

$ ls -l the two files CMake counts, and the core it does not
        209408  OnnxInference.ofx
      12400160  onnxruntime-ofx.dll
     673741344  onnxruntime_providers_cuda.dll
         22072  onnxruntime_providers_shared.dll

  provider + shared = 673763416 B = 642 MiB (integer division by 1048576)
  -> the '642 MB' is the provider itself; no CUDA runtime, no stale copy.

$ .validation/pe-sections.py <shipped provider>
